# UI and styling — nrscholar-frontend (web)

The web app mostly runs **inside the mobile WebView on phones**, used by children. Design mobile-first.

## Colors and tokens

- **[Standard]** Use the theme tokens in `tailwind.config.js` (a Material-style palette): `primary`, `primary-container`, `on-primary`, `secondary`, `secondary-container`, `tertiary`, `surface`, `surface-container-*`, `on-surface`, `on-surface-variant`, `outline`, `error`, …, plus the configured `fontFamily`.
- **[Avoid]** New arbitrary hex classes (`bg-[#141779]`, `text-[#464652]`). There are 1,500+ legacy ones, so don't add more. If a color isn't in the theme and is needed repeatedly, add a token to `tailwind.config.js` (in its own change, agreed with the designer).
- **[Avoid]** Inline `style={{…}}` for anything Tailwind can express. Keep it for dynamic values (progress widths, transforms, SVG math).
- Tailwind is **v3** (`tailwind.config.js`, `@tailwind` directives, `tailwindcss` PostCSS plugin). Don't write v4-only syntax. `@tailwindcss/postcss` v4 is installed but not used.

## Layout

- Mobile first: design for 360px, then scale up. No horizontal overflow. Use `min-h-[100dvh]`-style patterns instead of raw `100vh` (mobile WebView address-bar issues).
- Touch targets ≥ 44px, with generous spacing for small fingers.
- Respect safe areas when content is near the screen edges.
- Wrap screens in the shared `Layout` where the existing screens do.

## Reuse

- Characters and animations: `DragonCharacter`, `MonsterCharacter`, `InteractiveCompanion`, `LottiePlayer`. Don't add new animation libraries (framer-motion, Lottie, tsparticles and three.js are already here).
- Icons: `lucide-react` only.
- Child switching: `ChildSwitcherModal`.
- When the same UI appears on 2+ screens (headers with a back button and notification bell, stat cards, XP/level badges, progress rings), extract it to `src/components/` instead of copying markup again.

## States

Every data view renders **loading** (skeleton or friendly animation), **error** (translated, kid-friendly text, retry button), **empty** (encouraging message + next action) and **data**. Buttons that trigger requests show a pending state and can't be double-tapped.

## Animation and 3D

- Keep animations short and purposeful. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for large or looping motion.
- three.js / `@react-three/fiber`, tsparticles and Lottie are heavy: only on lazy-loaded screens. Dispose of scenes and clear intervals and animation frames on unmount.

## Accessibility

- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons. Real `<button>`s for actions. `alt` text on images (`alt=""` if decorative).
- Sufficient contrast. Don't rely on color alone for right/wrong answers. Add an icon or text.
- Text sizes readable for children (avoid tiny text below `text-xs`).
